From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:48:02 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Upstream's watcher of the system's memory is not started on
 Windows 10 Mobile

When the system runs short of commit nsAvailableMemoryWatcher unloads a
background tab, and failing that tells the engine "low-memory", and later
that it is over. In a single process no tab can be unloaded (tabbrowser
discards remote browsers only), so all it did here was drive the engine's
memory-pressure state beside the port's own code, which rations what a
"low-memory" costs on the only main thread: a stop from the watcher would
turn the next cheap "ongoing" into a fresh "low-memory" with its full
collection. CreateAvailableMemoryWatcher returns the inert base under
GECKO_W10M, as upstream does on platforms without a watcher.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherWin.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherWin.cpp b/xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherWin.cpp
index 8b625c68c9..c526dbacfe 100644
--- a/xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherWin.cpp
+++ b/xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherWin.cpp
@@ -392,11 +392,22 @@ nsAvailableMemoryWatcher::Observe(nsISupports* aSubject, const char* aTopic,
 }
 
 already_AddRefed<nsAvailableMemoryWatcherBase> CreateAvailableMemoryWatcher() {
+#if defined(GECKO_W10M)
+  // Not on Windows 10 Mobile. What this watcher does when the system runs
+  // short of commit is unload a background tab, which in a single process
+  // never succeeds (tabbrowser discards remote browsers only), and failing
+  // that tell the engine "low-memory", and later that it is over. There the
+  // engine is told both by one place that rations what a "low-memory" costs
+  // on the only main thread (widget/headless/GeckoW10mMemoryPressure.cpp,
+  // from the phone's own limit on the app); a second voice would undo it.
+  return do_AddRef(new nsAvailableMemoryWatcherBase);
+#else
   RefPtr watcher(new nsAvailableMemoryWatcher);
   if (NS_FAILED(watcher->Init())) {
     return do_AddRef(new nsAvailableMemoryWatcherBase);  // fallback
   }
   return watcher.forget();
+#endif
 }
 
 }  // namespace mozilla
